---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LANG_TAGS, GA4_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
/** Date de la dernière réécriture de cette page (mise en place de GA4 et Clarity). */
const updated = displayDate('2026-10-05', LANG_TAGS[lang]);
const gaCookie = `_ga_${GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}`;
const title = 'Salary Calculator Cookies in Greece: Analytics and Clarity';
const description = 'Salary calculator cookies in Greece: none for the calculation, _ga and _ga_ set by Google Analytics 4, _clck and _clsk by Microsoft Clarity, how to block them.';
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: label('home', lang), path: route('home', lang) }, { name: label('cookies', lang), path: route('cookies', lang) }])]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: label('cookies', lang) }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies and similar technologies</h1>
    <p class="lead">This page completes the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. The salary, tax and benefit calculators need no cookie; the only cookies come from two audience measurement tools, Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics 4.</p>

    <h2>Categories</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Strictly necessary</td><td>none</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analytics (audience measurement)</td><td>active</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Advertising</td><td>none</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Cookies set</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Service</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>_clck</code></td><td>Microsoft Clarity</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_clsk</code></td><td>Microsoft Clarity</td><td>1 day</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>MUID</code>, <code>CLID</code></td><td>Microsoft (own domains, possibly)</td><td>up to 1 year</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics 4</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>{gaCookie}</code></td><td>Google Analytics 4</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> produces session recordings and heatmaps: where people click, how far they scroll, which pages they open. The amounts you type into a calculator are masked in the browser and are not sent. <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google Ireland Limited) counts page views, traffic sources, visit length, device type and approximate location, and keeps the data for 14 months. Both load when the page opens; there is no consent banner.</p>

    <h2>What about the link with my result?</h2>
    <p>After you change a field, the calculator writes the values into the page address so you can share the calculation. That is not a cookie, and the address update is not passed to the analytics tools: nothing stays on your device beyond ordinary browsing history.</p>

    <h2>How to refuse analytics cookies</h2>
    <p>As the site asks for no consent, switching measurement off is done in your browser: block third-party cookies, block the domains <code>clarity.ms</code> and <code>google-analytics.com</code>, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. Clearing the site’s data removes cookies already set. The calculators keep working exactly as before.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Version of {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
